  "static_gate": "tests/test_window_caption_centring.py evaluates the v2 arithmetic for all 18 shipped frames with the shipped kwinrc at 380/480/720/1707 px, LTR/RTL, restored/maximized; it refuses old Bloom (-68, negative room at 388), old UI2 (+36), new frames with the old empty right side, and old 8 px spacer with the new buttons; restoring old kwinrc gives 19 failures and old Bloom rc 1 failure.",
  "retained_refusals": [
    "First private KWin attempt used KWIN_COMPOSE=Q: virtual 6.8.3 refused QPainter composition and kwin_wayland SIGSEGV'd on the first ScreenShot2 call (coredump PID 312633, private socket wayland-frames, app-code scope; core stored inaccessible). Later runs use O2 and RLIMIT_CORE=0; no further KWin core records.",
    "The first 150% English analysis mislabelled UI2 actions 'right' because the dark frame's bright top edge counted as caption ink; the image showed correct left actions. The per-row background detector fixes it and still fails every before/installed capture.",
    "The first --check evaluation treated an exact 0.0 offset as missing; corrected frame_failures() re-evaluates every saved run."
  ],
  "not_qualified": [
    "Signed image delivery and installed-session readback (owner reboot into a candidate carrying this source).",
    "Physical pointer/touch on the title bar and the spacer region; private KWin has no fake input here.",
